---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../consts";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How Heckers Software uses cookies and similar technologies on its website."
  lastUpdated="11 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how {COMPANY.name} ("we", "us", or "our") uses
    cookies and similar technologies on our website. It should be read together
    with our <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that are placed on your device when you visit a
    website. They are widely used to make websites work, or work more
    efficiently, as well as to provide information to the site owners. Similar
    technologies such as pixels and local storage may be used for comparable
    purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Types of cookies we use</h2>

  <h3>Consent-based cookies</h3>
  <p>
    We do not load any cookie-setting third-party scripts until you accept
    cookies via our consent banner. Once you accept, we may load
    <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, which we use to protect our contact
    form from spam and automated abuse and which may set a cookie for that
    purpose. If you decline, Turnstile is not loaded.
  </p>

  <h3>Functional cookies</h3>
  <p>
    Our newsletter subscription form, provided by our email service provider,
    may set cookies when you actively submit the form to sign up. These support
    the sign-up and delivery of the newsletter you requested.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Managing your consent</h2>
  <p>
    When you first visit our website, a small banner lets you accept or decline
    cookies. You can change your choice at any time using the
    <strong>"Cookie settings"</strong> link in the footer of any page. If you
    decline or later withdraw consent, the affected features (such as the
    contact form's spam protection) may not be available.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Some cookies are placed by third-party services that appear on our pages. We
    do not control these cookies. The main third parties we use are:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Cloudflare Turnstile</td>
        <td>Protecting the contact form against spam and automated abuse</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Newsletter provider</td>
        <td>Managing newsletter sign-ups and delivery</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>5. Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Most web browsers also allow you to control cookies through their settings.
    You can set your browser to refuse cookies or to alert you when cookies are
    being sent. Please note that if you disable or refuse cookies, some parts of
    this website may become inaccessible or not function properly. For more
    information on how to manage cookies, visit
    <a href="https://www.aboutcookies.org" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutcookies.org</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. The version published on
    this page, with the "Last updated" date shown above, is the version in
    effect.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about our use of cookies, please contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
